EXT. ICE-LOCKED LIFEBOAT, ARCTIC FLOE - DAWN

A battered orange lifeboat frozen into a plain of pack ice. White sky. White ground. The only color: the boat, four parkas, and a thin line of red blood on the ice.

CAPTAIN BRYNHILD OLSEN-ADESANYA (50s, frost in her eyebrows, a compass on a lanyard) crouches at the stern, rationing biscuits. Across from her, FIRST MATE HIRAM DELACROIX-NWOSU (40s, one glove missing) sits staring at his bare hand. At the bow, COOK YOSEFINA "FINA" LARSEN-OKAFOR (30s) feeds a tin stove with the last of the splinters. And curled in the bottom of the boat, wrapped in a tarp, lies deckhand TEMPERANCE BRIGGS-MOHAMMED (20s), breathing shallowly.

BRYNHILD
Nine biscuits. Four of us.

FINA
Two and a quarter each.

BRYNHILD
Two each. The quarter goes to Temperance.

HIRAM
She won't eat it.

BRYNHILD
She will.

Temperance stirs. Her eyelids flutter.

TEMPERANCE
(hoarse)
Is it morning?

FINA
It's morning.

TEMPERANCE
Is it warm?

FINA
(gently)
No, love.

A silence. The stove ticks. The wind picks up, sliding a ribbon of snow across the floe.

Hiram's head lifts. He cocks it, listening.

HIRAM
Do you hear that?

BRYNHILD
Hear what?

HIRAM
An engine.

They all go still. Far off, a faint drone. Fina laughs, one cracked note.

FINA
It's the wind.

HIRAM
It's an engine, Fina.

Brynhild stands, shading her eyes. A dark speck on the horizon, growing. Temperance grips the tarp. Then the speck resolves into a long gray shape with a red cross on its flank, and the drone swells into the unmistakable thrum of a rescue helicopter.

Nobody cheers. Nobody moves. Then Hiram begins to weep, and Fina puts her arm around him, and Brynhild picks up the flare gun with a hand that will not stop shaking.
